TASK:{"title":"AERO9500 Preliminary Report (Part 1)","overview":"Plan a simple space mission that benefits Australia and present preliminary design work to guide the full mission assignment. Explain the mission concept and rationale, plan how the assignment will be completed, identify information sources and software, and show evidence of technical progress."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Mission concept and rationale — What will it do, who are the users, why is it needed?","weight":40,"max":40,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"A clear and complete description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Clearly relates required mission function to users and their needs. References to literature as appropriate."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Sufficient description of mission goals, objectives, and requirements. Identification of users and their needs. Descriptions feature lack of specific details and/or incomplete referencing."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"A poor description with mission goals, objectives and requirements unclear. Insufficient identification of users and their needs."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Project plan — How you plan to complete the assignment, including either a Gantt chart or a timetable and information sources you plan to use","weight":30,"max":30,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The plan for project completion is robust and has provision for project variations and contingencies. The plan fits within the narrative set out by the mission concept – the student makes clear why the plan is developed this way in the context of the mission. Appropriate references to information sources are included."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Plan is presented but lacks some detail. However, the plan is enough to believe that the project is feasible."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"Plan is not included or does not have sufficient detail to demonstrate that the project can be completed."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Preliminary progress — Technical content and evidence of sufficient work done to date","weight":10,"max":10,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"Good preliminary set of results included with brief description and/or interpretation. Clearly on track for completion."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Minor work completed on the project. Results description or interpretation may be insufficient."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"No actual or useful work completed."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Report presentation","weight":20,"max":20,"levels":[{"label":"Accomplished","min":7,"max":10,"desc":"The document follows a clear and logical structure. The report is very easy to read: well-written, with good spelling and grammar, and appropriate language style. All aspects of formatting are consistent throughout the document. Graphical and tabular presentation of data is appropriate, clear and consistent. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are cited properly."},{"label":"Adequate","min":4,"max":6,"desc":"Document is not at a professional level but does make use of headings and subheadings to indicate document structure. The report may be difficult to read: writing is just ok, broad idea comes across; spelling and grammar have some flaws, not quite appropriate language style. Although figures and tables are labelled, the formatting is unclear and/or inconsistent to the extent that the reader can lose track of the context when reading. References in text match reference list (and vice versa) and are mostly cited correctly."},{"label":"Deficient","min":0,"max":3,"desc":"The document is poorly structured, is not coherent or shows a lack of understanding of the purpose of its sections. Much effort is required to read and understand the report: writing is poor, many mistakes with spelling and grammar, and possibly inappropriate language style (e.g. too informal). Presentation is poor to the extent that it impedes reading of the document. Examples include inconsistent formatting, and unlabelled figures or tables. References are either not cited or cited inconsistently."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"yes","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R2","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R3","met":"yes","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Image 1"},{"id":"R5","met":"partial","where":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","issue":"A 600 km orbit is low Earth orbit, not geostationary. Geostationary altitude is approximately 35,786 km above the equator; moreover, a geostationary satellite cannot remain directly overhead of the Great Barrier Reef, which is south of the equator."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","issue":"The stated 2016 and 2017 coral-loss percentages appear to conflate bleaching extent with coral mortality and are presented as whole-reef losses without qualification. Verify the figures and distinguish bleaching from mortality and local from reef-wide estimates."}],"overall":"The report communicates a relevant Australian mission need, identifies users, and provides a useful initial work plan. Its main weakness is the lack of preliminary engineering results, compounded by a fundamental error in the proposed orbit. Clarifying mission performance needs, correcting the orbit, and adding initial calculations or STK outputs would substantially strengthen the submission.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":24.0,"max":40.0,"reasoning":"The need, intended users, and general monitoring function are clear and supported by sources. However, mission objectives and requirements remain broad: the report does not specify sensor capabilities, coverage, revisit, data products, or measurable performance targets.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"A near-real-time relay to monitoring stations on the ground would allow marine and conservation scientists to more accurately predict and react to coral bleaching events."},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"This tool could be applied to a new satellite over the Great Barrier Reef."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":18.0,"max":30.0,"reasoning":"The Gantt chart and task descriptions provide a feasible sequence and include launch, orbit, ground control, communications, and STK work. The plan has little contingency provision, planned information sources are not comprehensively identified, and the stated editing weeks conflict with the chart, which places finalisation in weeks 9–10.","evidence":[{"where":"Image 1","quote":""},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"In addition to my own research, the syllabus work on astrodynamics will help me to understand and design an optimal mission."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"Weeks 7 and 8 are reserved for review, amendments, final simulations, and reflection."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Deficient","mark":3.0,"scale":10.0,"points":3.0,"max":10.0,"reasoning":"The report shows background reading and software tutorials, but includes no useful calculations, simulation results, or preliminary design outputs. The one specific orbital proposal is physically inconsistent, so it does not provide reliable technical progress.","evidence":[{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"My current choice is a geostationary orbit at an altitude of 600 km, which keeps the satellite fixed above the reef at all times."},{"where":"Project Plan & Preliminary Progress","quote":"also completed STK tutorials 1, 2, 3 & 4."}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Adequate","mark":6.0,"scale":10.0,"points":12.0,"max":20.0,"reasoning":"The report is logically sectioned and readable, and the Gantt chart is legible and labelled. The prose is occasionally informal, the references are presented as URLs rather than a consistently formatted reference list, and the schedule inconsistency reduces clarity. Overall, presentation is adequate but not fully professional.","evidence":[{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"Mission Concept & Rationale"},{"where":"Image 1","quote":""},{"where":"Mission Concept & Rationale","quote":"¹ https://www.noaa.gov/education/resource-collections/ocean-coasts/ocean-acidification"}]}]}
